# Phase 18 factory zero-pool getClient parity

- Recorded: 2026-10-23 10:38:25 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Source revision before this change: `95c49f8c`
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1, `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`

## Finding and change

Pinned Java `MQClientAPIFactory.getClient()` calls
`ThreadLocalRandom.nextInt(clients.length)` when the array length is not one.
For a started zero-client pool it throws `IllegalArgumentException`. Rust
returns `MQClientApiFactoryError::EmptyClientArray`; the factory test now
compares this typed outcome against the invoked Java exception fixture.

`fixtures/runtime/api-factory.json` now also records
`zeroClientGetClientError=IllegalArgumentException`. SHA-256:
`fcbb745a4eab18d4fa8e5163fa69deeffa935375b660fde8e915c7dab9e2da38`.

